# Default parameters for Raspberry Pi Pico 2 (RP2350) ArduPilot port.
# Battery monitoring defaults are set as compile-time defines in hwdef.dat
# (HAL_BATT_VOLT_SCALE=10.1, HAL_BATT_CURR_SCALE=17.0) and do not need
# to be overridden here.
#
# Reduce main loop rate from the default 400 Hz to 350 Hz.
# The RP2350 Cortex-M33 @ 150 MHz cannot sustain the full 400 Hz task
# budget: extra_loop_us accumulates and GCS update_send() tasks are
# starved of time_available, silencing all MAVLink output.  350 Hz
# gives ~2857 µs per loop (vs 2500 µs at 400 Hz), enough headroom for
# the GCS and logging tasks to execute each cycle.
SCHED_LOOP_RATE 350

# Uncomment and adjust to match your power brick or current sensor:
#BATT_AMP_PERVLT 17.0
#BATT_VOLT_MULT 10.1
